    "description": "Both were on the Operator mockup and both moved to Deal on Aug 13. Deal is the right grain because they vary by market.\n\n=== FIELDS ===\n\n* Default Redirect URL — URL — the middle-layer redirect destination. Ops overrides per link on the Link record; Deal holds the default.\n\n* Pitch & Positioning — Salesforce File on Deal — the deck showing what was promised to the operator for that market.\n\n=== IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS ===\n\n* Redirect: removed from Operator (BUILD-127). Rationale — 'if it's like Canada versus US, I think that the URL is different.' Override at Link level: 'when we get down link by link, that's where the operations team can override it sometimes.'\n\n* Pitch: Salesforce Files, not Drive. Joyce: 'that should be a file that you save in Salesforce, not Google.'\n\n* Multiple pitches per operator across markets is normal; one multi-market deck can be uploaded to several Deals. Emily: 'when I did the BetMGM one, it included both Alberta and Ontario, but we can always just upload it twice.'\n\n* Neither exists on Deal today — Kobi: 'We don't have this on a deal right now, no.'\n\n=== NOTES ===\n\n* Joyce's reasoning for the pitch move: 'when we go to enable a deal, we want this as a reference to be like, what did we actually promise the operator?'\n\n=== SOURCE ===\n\n* Aug 13 call — redirect removed from Operator, pitch moved to Deal\n\nDependencies: None\n\nOwner (proposed): TBD\n\nRemember to update the requirements documentation as part of this change.\n\nCreated 2026-08-17 from the Operator/Partner ticket review, approved by Kobi.",
